  "notes": [
    "Fully regular -AR verb; follows standard endings throughout",
    "Past participle: molestado (regular)",
    "Like *gustar*, often used with indirect object pronouns: *me molesta* = it bothers me, *le molesta* = it bothers him/her",
    "*Me molesta que* + subjuntivo = it bothers me that: *Me molesta que llegues tarde* = It bothers me that you arrive late",
    "*Molestar a alguien* = to bother/disturb someone: *No me molestes* = Don't bother me",
    "*Molestarse en* + infinitivo = to bother to do something: *Ni se molestó en llamar* = He didn't even bother to call",
    "*Molestarse* (reflexive) = to take offence: *Se molestó cuando le dije la verdad* = He took offence when I told him the truth",
    "Related: la molestia (bother, trouble, annoyance), molesto (annoying, bothered), molestar (noun: nuisance)"
  ],
  "sourceFile": "Verbs/m/Molestar.md"
